 ## Overview
-Material-Based Volumetric Emission encompasses display techniques that generate visible voxels within a physical medium through fluorescence, upconversion, or photochromism [S1, S2, unofficial]. It differs from sibling methods like [Galvanometer Scanner Volume Rendering](5277-galvanometer-scanner-volume-rendering.md) by defining voxels through material excitation rather than beam scanning, and from [Holographic Computer-Generated Holography (CGH) Calculation](6884-holographic-computer-generated-holography-cgh-calculation.md) by relying on physical light emission rather than interference pattern calculation.
